  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong uptrend (e.g., Example 1), consistently overestimating the 30-day target by 5-10 EUR despite volatile sentiment.",
    "Forecast fails to account for mean reversion; after a sharp price spike in the last 2 days, the model continues its linear ascent while true outcomes drop significantly below the forecast path.",
    "Sentiment history (values near 0.00) provides no corrective signal for the model, which ignores negative sentiment spikes (-0.25/-0.20) that precede immediate price drops in the true outcome.",
    "The model assumes a smooth linear trajectory and lacks volatility adjustment; it fails to capture the high-frequency oscillations seen in the true outcomes (e.g., Example 4 and 5).",
    "When the last 3 days show a net positive trend, apply a downward correction factor of approximately 6-8% to the model's 30-day forecast target.",
    "If sentiment history contains negative values within the last 10 days, reduce the forecasted growth rate by half regardless of recent price momentum."
  ]
}
